# Nothing on this page is exempt: every example that documents an output block is replayed.
#
# The three `journalctl -f` examples document no output, because -f blocks until interrupted
# and a batch would only capture whatever had arrived before the timeout killed it. They are
# named here rather than listed as entries, because an entry naming an example the harness never had
# is an error, since it would read as an exemption while exempting nothing.
#
#   Watch new entries arrive
#   Watch one service
#   Watch for errors across the whole machine
#
# Each was verified by hand in the sandbox: run it in one shell, restart backup-sync in
# another, and watch the entries appear.
